/* Help articles for the on-site guide. Generated by scripts/build_solutions.py; do not edit. */
window.BF_KB = [{"q":"How do I start?","a":"Open Studio and choose a worked example close to your field, or create a table and paste your data straight from Excel or an instrument export. Then press Analyze, or open Facet for a suggestion.","l":"studio/","t":"Getting started","k":"getting started"},{"q":"Which table type should I use?","a":"XY for curves and spectra (one X column, one or more Y columns; columns with the same title are replicates). Column for comparing groups. Multiple variables for compositions, process settings and properties, one row per sample.","l":"studio/","t":"Getting started","k":"getting started"},{"q":"Do I need an account?","a":"No. Everything runs in your browser and projects are kept there. An account adds cloud storage, your plan on every computer and Lab sharing.","l":"studio/","t":"Getting started","k":"getting started"},{"q":"Which equation should I fit?","a":"Run Auto-fit: it fits every plausible equation for the shape of your data and ranks them by AICc. Equation discovery can also find a formula that is not in the library.","l":"tools/curve-fitting/","t":"Curve fitting and equations","k":"curve fitting and equations"},{"q":"The fit does not converge.","a":"Check that X and Y are in the right columns and units, try Auto-fit, fix a parameter you know, or start from a simpler model. Very few points cannot support many parameters.","l":"tools/curve-fitting/","t":"Curve fitting and equations","k":"curve fitting and equations"},{"q":"Can I type my own equation?","a":"Yes. Choose User-defined equation and write it with x, any parameter names, + − * / ^ and functions such as exp, ln and sqrt.","l":"tools/curve-fitting/","t":"Curve fitting and equations","k":"curve fitting and equations"},{"q":"Which test should I use?","a":"Facet suggests one from your data: t test or Mann–Whitney for two groups, ANOVA, Welch’s ANOVA or Kruskal–Wallis for more. Lattent checks normality and equal variance for you.","l":"studio/?example=anova","t":"Statistics","k":"statistics"},{"q":"Why not several t tests?","a":"Each extra test raises the chance of a false positive. ANOVA with Tukey or Holm–Šidák post tests corrects for the number of comparisons.","l":"studio/?example=anova","t":"Statistics","k":"statistics"},{"q":"How is crystallite size calculated?","a":"Peaks are fitted with pseudo-Voigt profiles on a fitted baseline, instrumental broadening is removed, and the Scherrer and Williamson–Hall equations give size and strain. Sizes above about 100 nm are unreliable with any lab diffractometer.","l":"tools/xrd-crystallite-size/","t":"XRD, spectra and band gaps","k":"xrd, spectra and band gaps"},{"q":"How do I identify the phase?","a":"After a peak analysis with X as 2θ, press Identify phases and list the elements that may be present. Lattent matches your peaks against every computed structure of those elements.","l":"tools/xrd-crystallite-size/","t":"XRD, spectra and band gaps","k":"xrd, spectra and band gaps"},{"q":"My Tauc fit looks wrong.","a":"Choose the transition type (direct or indirect) and set the linear region by hand around the steepest part of the absorption edge.","l":"tools/xrd-crystallite-size/","t":"XRD, spectra and band gaps","k":"xrd, spectra and band gaps"},{"q":"What can Facet do without an API key?","a":"Suggest analyses, check your whole project for mistakes, and read data from a picture of a graph. All of this runs offline in your browser.","l":"ai/","t":"Facet and the AI models","k":"facet and the ai models"},{"q":"How do I use the chat?","a":"Open Facet, choose Ask, and add your own Anthropic or OpenAI key; it stays in your browser. You can attach a figure and ask what it shows or what is wrong with it. Analyses it proposes run only after you approve them.","l":"ai/","t":"Facet and the AI models","k":"facet and the ai models"},{"q":"How accurate are the models?","a":"Each model’s accuracy on data it never saw is listed on the AI page and the validation page.","l":"ai/","t":"Facet and the AI models","k":"facet and the ai models"},{"q":"The database search fails.","a":"Discover queries the public Alexandria database from your browser. Check your connection, or a network that blocks external sites, and try again; very broad searches can be slow.","l":"studio/?discover=search","t":"Discover: database, phases, new materials","k":"discover: database, phases, new materials"},{"q":"Are generated materials real discoveries?","a":"They are candidates: compositions predicted to be stable and close to your target band gap, and absent from the database. Confirm them with a calculation or a synthesis.","l":"studio/?discover=search","t":"Discover: database, phases, new materials","k":"discover: database, phases, new materials"},{"q":"How do I get a figure for my paper?","a":"Every chart has PNG export. Pro adds 600-dpi PNG and vector SVG without the watermark, plus methods, results and figure-legend text written from your numbers.","l":"studio/","t":"Figures, reports and export","k":"figures, reports and export"},{"q":"Can I export my results?","a":"Yes: results tables as CSV and one-page reports with Pro, and your data tables as CSV on any plan.","l":"studio/","t":"Figures, reports and export","k":"figures, reports and export"},{"q":"Where is my project saved?","a":"In your browser, automatically. Clearing your browser’s site data removes it, so save important work to the cloud (free account: 3 projects) or as a project file.","l":"account/","t":"Projects, cloud and Lab teams","k":"projects, cloud and lab teams"},{"q":"How does Lab sharing work?","a":"The Lab plan owner invites members from the account page; projects shared with the lab open for every member.","l":"account/","t":"Projects, cloud and Lab teams","k":"projects, cloud and lab teams"},{"q":"How do I pay?","a":"By card, PayPal or Apple Pay worldwide, by UPI, cards or net banking in India, or by invoice for institutions. See the pricing page.","l":"pricing/","t":"Plans and billing","k":"plans and billing"},{"q":"I paid, but Pro is still locked.","a":"Sign in with the same email you used to pay; the plan activates within a few seconds of the payment confirmation. If it does not, contact us with your receipt.","l":"pricing/","t":"Plans and billing","k":"plans and billing"},{"q":"How do I cancel or get a refund?","a":"Cancel any time from your account; you keep Pro until the end of the paid period. Refunds within 14 days of a payment, no questions asked.","l":"pricing/","t":"Plans and billing","k":"plans and billing"},{"q":"My pasted data lands in one column.","a":"Lattent recognises tab, comma and semicolon separators and decimal commas. If the paste still lands in one column, copy the cells directly from Excel rather than from a PDF, or use Paste or import.","l":"support/","t":"Troubleshooting","k":"troubleshooting problem error broken"},{"q":"A chart is blank or the page looks broken.","a":"Use a recent Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari, reload the page, and turn off extensions that block scripts for this site.","l":"support/","t":"Troubleshooting","k":"troubleshooting problem error broken"},{"q":"Studio is slow with a large file.","a":"Curve fitting and AutoML work best with up to a few thousand points; for long spectra, crop to the region of interest first.","l":"support/","t":"Troubleshooting","k":"troubleshooting problem error broken"},{"q":"I lost my project.","a":"Projects live in the browser where you made them. If the browser’s data was cleared and the project was not saved to the cloud or as a file, it cannot be recovered.","l":"support/","t":"Troubleshooting","k":"troubleshooting problem error broken"},{"q":"How do I identify the phases in my XRD pattern?","a":"Fit the peaks in Studio with X set to 2θ, then press Identify phases and list the elements that may be present. Lattent matches your peaks against every computed structure of those elements and flags peaks left unexplained.","l":"studio/?discover=phase","t":"Identify phases","k":"phase identification diffraction pattern xrd match crystal structure"},{"q":"How do I get the band gap from a UV–Vis spectrum?","a":"Paste wavelength (or energy) and absorbance into the band-gap tool. It builds the Tauc plot, finds the linear part of the absorption edge and reports the gap with a confidence interval.","l":"tools/band-gap-tauc/","t":"Band-gap tool","k":"tauc optical band gap uv vis absorbance edge"},{"q":"How do I get activation energy from conductivity or rate data?","a":"Use the activation-energy tool: paste temperature and conductivity (or rate constant) and Lattent fits Arrhenius or VFT and reports Eₐ in kJ/mol and eV with confidence intervals.","l":"tools/activation-energy-arrhenius/","t":"Activation-energy tool","k":"arrhenius activation energy conductivity rate temperature"},{"q":"Can Lattent suggest new materials?","a":"Yes, at the level of composition. The generator proposes formulas inside the elements you choose, steered towards a band gap, predicts stability and band gap with intervals, and checks each candidate against 5.8 million computed structures.","l":"studio/?discover=gen","t":"Generate materials","k":"generate new materials diffusion generative compositions discovery"},{"q":"Can Lattent write a report for me?","a":"Yes. Open Facet in Studio and choose Report. The agent plans the analyses, runs them, checks them for mistakes and assembles a report with methods, results, figures, checks and next steps. With your own AI key it also drafts the summary and discussion, and it can review figures you supply.","l":"studio/?example=anova&facet=report","t":"See an autonomous report","k":"report autonomous agent write up paper methods results export"},{"q":"Can Lattent read a graph from an image?","a":"Yes. In Facet, choose Graph: calibrate the axes with four clicks, click the curve, and Lattent traces it into a data table. With an AI key you can also attach the figure and ask what it shows or what is wrong with it.","l":"studio/?facet=graph","t":"Read a graph","k":"digitise digitize image plot picture figure graph data extract"},{"q":"What is Facet?","a":"Facet is Lattent’s AI lab partner. It suggests analyses, checks your project for mistakes, reads graphs, writes reports autonomously and, with your own Claude or GPT key, answers questions and reviews figures. All numbers come from the validated engine.","l":"ai/","t":"Facet AI","k":"facet ai assistant partner co-scientist"},{"q":"How much does Lattent cost?","a":"{{pricing}}","l":"pricing/","t":"See pricing","k":"price cost pro plan lab free subscription payment inr rupee"},{"q":"Is my data private?","a":"Analyses run in your browser and projects stay there unless you save them to the cloud. Nothing you paste is uploaded. The optional AI features send data only to the provider you chose, with your own key.","l":"legal/privacy.html","t":"Privacy notice","k":"privacy data upload security gdpr stored"},{"q":"How do I talk to a person?","a":"Use the contact form and tell us what you need. We usually reply within one working day.","l":"contact/","t":"Contact us","k":"contact email support human sales invoice question help"}];
